#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "CAP-AUDIT.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "Every data access and every administrative action is recorded with principal, object, action and time."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "A test read and a test grant both appear in audit."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "CAP-AUDIT.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "Audit is copied to a separate store with retention set by policy, beyond the platform's own retention, and is readable only by auditors."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "The copy holds records older than the platform's retention; a non-auditor read is refused."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "CAP-AUDIT.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "SHOULD"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "Query text is recorded only when a case needs it, because query text can contain personal data."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "Verbose audit is off by default; turning it on is a reviewed change."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "CAP-AUDIT.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "Access to identifiable or special-category records (T3, T4) records a purpose chosen from a declared list, as well as principal, object, action and time.{1}*Example:* An officer opens a learner's support plan and chooses the purpose 'case review'; the audit row records the purpose with the officer, the record and the time."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "Audit rows for T3 and T4 reads carry a purpose."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "CAP-AUDIT.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "Anomalous access to T3 and T4 data (unusual volume, time or scope outside the entitlement) raises an alert."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-audit.md
msgid "A simulated out-of-scope read raises an alert."
msgstr ""

